"}]},"type":"ListItem"},{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"workbench.views.noMatches"},"tone":"muted","value":"pay","variant":"label","visible":false},"id":"views-no-matches","type":"Text"},{"config":{"text":{"$i18n":"workbench.views.emptyTitle"},"tone":"muted","variant":"label","visible":false},"id":"views-empty","type":"Text"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"Stack"}]},"type":"RootShell"},"name":"Widget tree","spec":{"accessibility":["A finding is never conveyed by its dot alone: the dot carries the text \"Has an error finding\" or \"Has a warning finding\", and the comment count its own sentence, for assistive technology.","The tree is a labelled landmark (\"Widget tree of the selected View\") with the keyboard navigation of a tree; C comments on the focused row."],"constraints":["Built only from Adapter Widgets (Stack, Text, Icon, Badge, Button, TextInput, ListItem, Kbd, Alert, EmptyState); no Widget outside the Adapter catalog.","There is no filter or search in the app's Widget tree, so none is modelled for it; the filter belongs to the View list that All Views opens, which its Variants show (it matches the View name or its feature tag).","Collapsing is shown by a Variant that hides the rows below a branch; the expansion is not interactive, and indentation is the ListItem level (16px per level, the app indents 10px).","The hover look of a row, its focus ring, the keyboard navigation of the tree (arrows, Home, End), the sideways scroll of a deep tree and the sidebar's own navigation are not modelled; the context menu is a floating card placed under the rows.","Every visible string is bound with $i18n except identities (Widget types and ids); en-US and zh-TW keep identical key sets.","Visual language follows the Quiet Canvas design system in DESIGN.md."],"decisions":[],"entryConditions":["A member opened a View in the Workbench; the sidebar shows All Views, the View name and the Widget tree below them, 264px wide at the left edge (resizable from 220px to 360px); a tablet shows a 56px icon rail and opens the full sidebar as a slide-over, and a phone opens it from the menu, so below 640px this View fills the width.","The base state is the View Checkout with every branch expanded and the Button #checkout-submit selected: two unresolved comments and a warning finding on it, one comment on #card-number, an error finding on #error-banner.","The render context selects one Workspace viewport preset, one Locale and one theme."],"intent":"Show the Widget tree of the Workbench sidebar as built from Adapter Widgets only: the selected View's whole Widget hierarchy as rows (type glyph, type, and the Widget id of the selected row), with the unresolved comment count and the Checks finding of each Widget, a branch chevron, and the notices for a missing or unavailable tree; and, behind All Views, the View list with its filter.","interactionRules":["Every Widget of the View is a row, at any depth, indented by depth; picking a row selects the Widget in the canvas and the Inspector, and a Widget picked in the canvas expands the branches above its row.","A row that has children shows a chevron at its end, pointing up while the branch is expanded and down while it is collapsed; a Widget whose content Slot is empty gets a note, \"No Widgets in content yet\".","The Widget id shows beside the type on the selected row (and on a hovered or touched row); the unresolved Review threads anchored on the Widget are counted next to it in the annotation color, and the worst Checks finding that resolves to it is a dot, red for an error and amber for a warning, each with a text alternative.","A Widget can be chosen as a comment target from the tree without pointing into the Preview: pressing C on a focused row, or the row's context menu entry \"Comment on this Widget\", starts a comment on it; neither is offered to a member who may not comment, nor on a phone.","All Views replaces the tree with the list of the Workspace's Views under a Filter Views field that matches the name or the feature tag; each row names the View, shows its feature tag in mono and, when the View has diagnostics, a warning count; the open View is marked, and a filter that matches nothing says so.","A selection that names a Widget the View no longer has is reported by a persistent inline notice above the tree until the context is replaced or left; a View whose structure cannot be read shows \"No Widget tree\" with the reason."],"references":[{"label":"Phase 5 of the closed loop: dogfood coverage of the core surfaces","relation":"decision","type":"external","uri":"https://github.com/DevilTea/uiux/discussions/379#discussioncomment-19257377"},{"relation":"opened-from","type":"view","viewId":"7f3d7780-3cb9-4e57-8f0b-2e8d569905c1"},{"relation":"sibling","type":"view","viewId":"b1c7e301-4a1d-4c2e-9f31-7a4c0d2e6b01"}],"requirements":["01a116f0-94ea-7b74-a773-12147804a393","01a11658-1f97-7ea9-9715-e29d45ccb09d","01a1144e-513d-7cf2-8e18-4a6f4494665b"]},"variants":{"branch-collapsed":{"state":{"row-card-cvc":{"visible":false},"row-card-expiry":{"visible":false},"row-card-meta-row":{"visible":false},"row-card-number":{"visible":false},"row-checkout-back":{"visible":false},"row-checkout-submit":{"visible":false},"row-error-banner":{"visible":false},"row-form-title":{"visible":false},"row-payment-form":{"expanded":false},"row-payment-form-chev-closed":{"visible":true},"row-payment-form-chev-open":{"visible":false}}},"collapsed-to-top":{"requirements":["01a116f0-89b6-7d08-a850-e1ee1aecd51f"],"state":{"row-card-cvc":{"visible":false},"row-card-expiry":{"visible":false},"row-card-meta-row":{"visible":false},"row-card-number":{"visible":false},"row-checkout-back":{"visible":false},"row-checkout-header":{"visible":false},"row-checkout-submit":{"selected":false,"visible":false},"row-checkout-submit-id":{"visible":false},"row-checkout-title":{"visible":false},"row-error-banner":{"visible":false},"row-form-title":{"visible":false},"row-order-summar